.TH ACC 1 2026-10-22 "ACC" "ACC Manual"
.SH NAME
acc \- start here: attach to the ACC collective, or run the stack
.SH SYNOPSIS
.B acc
.RB [ \-\-workspace
.IR dir " | " \fB\-\-no\-workspace\fR ]
.RB [ \-\-no\-probe ]
.RB [ \-\-profile
.IR profile ]
.RB [ \-\-resume
.RI [ session_id ]]
.br
.B acc
.B \-\-list\-sessions
.br
.B acc stack
.RB { up | down | status " | ...}"
.RI [ args ...]
.br
.B acc
.RB { doctor | setup }
.RI [ args ...]
.br
.B acc
.RB { paths | tour }
.br
.B acc
.RB { \-\-version | \-\-help }
.SH DESCRIPTION
.B acc
is the one command an operator starts with on a host where ACC (Agentic
Cell Corpus) is installed.
Alone, it attaches the terminal UI,
.BR acc-tui (1),
to the running collective.
When nothing answers on the bus it says so in one line and exits 3 rather
than drawing an empty screen.
.PP
The first
.B acc
on a host with no configuration anywhere runs the guided setup
(\fBacc\-cli setup\fR) and then the first-run tour.
.SS Workspaces
Started in a directory,
.B acc
proposes that directory as the session's workspace and asks once whether it
is trusted:
.TP
.B y
Trust this directory for this session only; nothing is recorded.
.TP
.B always
Trust this directory and record it.
.TP
.B below
Trust it and every directory below it, and record it.
A directory holding many repositories asks for confirmation first.
.TP
.BR n ", " never
Deny it and record that, so it is not asked again
(\fBacc\-cli workspace revoke\fR asks again).
.TP
.RB "Enter (the default " N )
No workspace this time; nothing is recorded.
.PP
A trusted directory rides the session as \fBACC_WORKSPACE_HOST_DIR\fR and
.B acc stack up
mounts it into the cells at \fI/workspace\fR.
A directory never trusted is never mounted, never read by a file skill and
never selected.
The record is kept in \fI~/.config/acc/trust.yaml\fR and managed with
.BR "acc\-cli workspace" .
.SH OPTIONS
.TP
.BI \-\-workspace " dir"
Use \fIdir\fR as the session's workspace (still subject to trust).
.TP
.B \-\-no\-workspace
Ask nothing and attach without a workspace.
.TP
.B \-\-no\-probe
Do not check that a collective answers on the bus before starting the TUI.
.TP
.BR \-\-profile ", " \-\-resume ", " \-\-list\-sessions
Passed through to
.BR acc-tui (1).
.TP
.BR \-V ", " \-\-version
Print the version and exit.
.TP
.BR \-h ", " \-\-help
Print a short usage and exit.
.SH COMMANDS
.TP
.BI "stack " args...
Run the packaged deploy script,
.BR acc-deploy (1),
with \fIargs\fR (\fBup\fR, \fBdown\fR, \fBstatus\fR, \fBlogs\fR, ...).
On \fBup\fR, \fBstart\fR and \fBrebuild\fR, a trusted current directory is
mounted as the workspace.
Needs
.BR bash (1);
on Windows use Podman Desktop or WSL.
.TP
.BI "doctor " args...
The same as
.BR "acc\-cli doctor" :
a read-only report of deployment health.
.TP
.BI "setup " args...
The same as
.BR "acc\-cli setup" :
the guided first-run configuration.
.TP
.B paths
Print where this host's ACC lives \(em the configuration home, the data
share and the state root \(em and why each was chosen.
.TP
.B tour
Start the TUI with the first-run tour again.
.SH HOST LAYOUT
Every ACC command finds its files with the same rule, so a command works
from any directory, not only inside a checkout.
An environment variable always wins.
.TP
.B home
The operator's configuration: \fB$ACC_HOME\fR; else \fI~/.config/acc\fR
when it holds \fIacc\-config.yaml\fR; else \fI/etc/acc\fR when it does;
else the checkout the current directory is in.
.TP
.B share
The read-only data trees (roles, skills, mcps, collectives, container):
\fB$ACC_SHARE\fR; else the home when it carries \fIroles/\fR; else the tree
shipped inside the installed package; else \fI/usr/share/acc\fR; else the
checkout.
.TP
.B state
What is written at runtime: \fB$ACC_STATE\fR; else \fI/var/lib/acc\fR for
the system configuration; else \fI$XDG_STATE_HOME/acc\fR
(\fI~/.local/state/acc\fR) for a per-user one; else the checkout.
.PP
On an RPM install the system state is shared with the \fBacc\fR service
user through the \fBacc\fR group; join it with
\fBusermod \-aG acc\fR \fIuser\fR to install packages the service runs.
.SH ENVIRONMENT
.TP
.B ACC_NATS_URL
The bus to probe and attach to (default \fBnats://localhost:4222\fR).
.TP
.BR ACC_HOME ", " ACC_SHARE ", " ACC_STATE
Override the layout above.
.TP
.B ACC_DEPLOY_SCRIPT
The deploy script \fBacc stack\fR runs.
.TP
.B ACC_WORKSPACE_HOST_DIR
The session's workspace; set by \fBacc\fR when one is trusted.
.SH FILES
.TP
.I /etc/acc
The system configuration: \fIacc\-config.yaml\fR, \fImodels.yaml\fR,
\fIcollective.yaml\fR, \fIcatalogs.yaml\fR and the secrets in \fIacc.env\fR.
.TP
.I ~/.config/acc
A per-user configuration, used before \fI/etc/acc\fR when it holds
\fIacc\-config.yaml\fR.
.TP
.I ~/.config/acc/trust.yaml
Trusted and denied workspace directories.
.TP
.I /usr/share/acc
The data trees shipped with the package.
.TP
.I /var/lib/acc
Shared state: packages, instances, workspaces, logs, sessions, trace.
.SH EXIT STATUS
.TP
.B 0
Success.
.TP
.B 2
Unknown option, or \fBacc stack\fR cannot find its script or bash.
.TP
.B 3
No collective answers on \fBACC_NATS_URL\fR.
.PP
\fBdoctor\fR, \fBsetup\fR and \fBstack\fR return the exit status of the
command they run.
.SH EXAMPLES
.nf
acc stack up            # bring the collective up
acc                     # attach the TUI, offering this directory as workspace
acc \-\-no\-workspace      # attach without one
acc doctor              # what is wrong, if anything
acc paths               # which files this host uses, and why
.fi
.SH SEE ALSO
.BR acc-tui (1),
.BR acc-cli (1),
.BR acc-pkg (1),
.BR acc-deploy (1),
.BR acc-webgui (1),
.BR acc-agent (1),
.BR acc-catalog (1)
